// app_ext.at — the demo ext PORT anchor (PLAN-047 T2). The stable name that
// callers reference: on the VM target the Plan 442 A3 adapter chain resolves
// this file to its sibling app_ext.vm.at (GENERATED from content.ts by
// scripts/gen-vm-content.mjs — see the chain in auto-lang ext_stubs.rs:
// X.at → X.vm.at → X.web.at). On the vue target this file is never loaded:
// the SFC keeps importing the hand-written app_ext.ts (the bridge + log
// helpers + the content.ts-reading initial_content), and auto-man's ext copy
// is fed by the widget use block only. Deliberately code-free — the port has
// exactly one implementation per track and neither is written here.
//
// Plan 424 pure-forwarding port declaration (added PLAN-051 T6): newer
// auto-man transpilers reject a use-block `.at` fn module with neither
// top-level fns nor use.web bindings ("declares no top-level fns…"), which
// aborted the vue project generation mid-flight (child widget SFCs and the
// vue-tsc gate silently skipped). This forwarding declaration is the
// sanctioned code-free form — the vue transpile turns it into a re-export
// of the real app_ext.ts symbol, and the VM chain still resolves X.vm.at
// FIRST (ext_stubs.rs resolve_vm_at_adapter order), so the adapter twin
// below keeps winning untouched.
use.web.fn initial_content from "src/front/utils/app_ext.ts"
